Scope check ({{ scope_guard }}):
- Before the first change, note the base with `git status --porcelain=v2 --branch --untracked-files=all`:
  its `# branch.oid` line is the commit you start from, and the files it lists are already
  modified — the user's edits.
- When you delegate a change, tell the subagent making it: change only what the task needs; list
  other improvements in your report instead of making them.
- When every change is done (with Agent Teams, every task), call {{ scope_guard }} before any review{% if adversary %} and before {{ adversary }}{% endif %}.
{% if implementer_isolated -%}
- {{ implementer }} works in its own git worktree: merge its branch into the working branch before
  every call to {{ scope_guard }}, or {{ scope_guard }} checks code without the change.
{% endif -%}
- Give {{ scope_guard }} the goal and the latest approved plan or brief, verbatim, with its acceptance
  criteria; the decisions the user confirmed during the work; the base and the already-modified
  files;{% if formatter %} the formatter that runs after every edit (`{{ formatter }}`);{% endif %} and the findings the team fixed.
- Cuts (`Verdict: TRIM`, or any Cut list): reverting them is the one edit you make yourself. Do
  exactly what each cut says and write nothing new: restore the lines to the base, restore a whole
  file with `git checkout <base> -- <path>`, or delete a new file. Then run the tests; if a revert
  breaks one, undo that revert and record the cut as kept, with the failure.
- Gaps (`Verdict: INCOMPLETE`): send {{ implementer if implementer else "the subagent that made the change" }} only the Partial and Missing items,
  verbatim, with the plan text they come from. Then call {{ scope_guard }} once more on the whole
  change from the same base, and revert any new cuts it lists. At most {{ rounds }} completion round{% if rounds != 1 %}s{% endif %}:
  an item still Partial or Missing after that is reported as not done, never as done.
- Differs: don't rework it; put it in the final report for the user to accept or reject.
- If the report has no `Verdict:` line, call {{ scope_guard }} once more; if it still has none, report
  the scope check as not done.
- Subagents can't call each other: only you pass items between {{ scope_guard }} and
  {{ implementer if implementer else "the subagent that made the change" }}.
- In the final report, give the plan coverage, the blast radius, every cut (reverted, or kept with
  its reason), every Differs, the Defer list as follow-ups, and that fixes made after this check
  weren't traced against the plan.
{%- endif %}
